■ ☐ White/blue hierarchy is controlled
■ ☐ Cross-tower sightline remains clear
■ ☐ Glass is readable rather than mirror-heavy
■ ☐ One or two graphics do more work than many decals
■ ☐ Mundane office layer is present
■ ☐ No cyberpunk greeble drift
GRAPHICS / UI
■ ☐ Spacing and hierarchy feel intentional
■ ☐ Blue/cyan used as system, not decoration
■ ☐ Microtype remains secondary
■ ☐ Legal/corporate tone stays straight
■ ☐ No default vaporwave gradients
■ ☐ Typography is clean and legible
PROP / WEAPON
■ ☐ Silhouette communicates function instantly
■ ☐ Material palette belongs to office/corporate future
■ ☐ Detail survives distance and motion
■ ☐ Physics/destruction state remains readable
■ ☐ No tactical-shooter clutter unless function demands it
OPEN PRODUCTION ITEMS
22  OPEN QUESTIONS / TBD

The following areas should not be treated as fully locked until they have been tested in-engine. They are 
intentionally separated from the approved visual pillars so collaborators do not accidentally turn experiments into 
permanent rules.
