+# Office kit detail · Round 3
+
+**Status:** Target for Alex’s review · **Last updated:** 2026-11-12
+
+[Contact sheet](contact_sheet_r3.png) · [Governing brief](FEEDBACK_02.md) · [Exact prompt set](prompts_r3.json) · 
[200 px direction check](thumbnail_check_r3.png)
+
+Five families, ten directions, twenty concept views, generated with the built-in ImageGen tool.
+Each sheet puts A on the left and B on the right, hero above and rival below, with a one-line caption for each 
direction.
+The hero brief is 1,700 mm eye height; the rival brief is 12,000 mm across the street, covering three floors.
+These are visual concepts, not measured drawings or engine captures: the dimensions below govern modelling, rather 
than measurements inferred from painted perspective.
+Camera distance, mesh bounds and two-pane visibility have not been measured in Unity.
+
+The main reference is [bible plate 04](../Office/refs/bible_ref_04.png): folded white masses, whole cobalt faces, 
dark slots and a strong three-floor rhythm.
+The other three bible plates informed restrained graphic composition, and the [atrium 
plate](../Office/refs/plate_law_firm_atrium.png) informed materials and depth.
+Round 2’s [contact sheet](contact_sheet_r2.png) and [README](README_r2.md), the approved office paintings, the Unity 
office captures, the kit dimensions and glass specification were reviewed before generation.
+[FEEDBACK_02.md](FEEDBACK_02.md) takes precedence over the earlier briefs.
+
+## Modelling boundaries
+
+All moves below are proposed visual variants inside the existing outer envelopes, with the original pivots, snap 
ends, floor/soffit contact lands and colliders retained.
+No new projection is needed; the permitted ceiling remains 15 mm, away from snap and contact faces.
+Preserve the 4,000 mm bay, 600 mm façade sill, 4,300 mm floor-to-soffit height, 4,500 mm storey, 200 mm slab and 
1,200 × 2,400 mm service opening.
+Recess depths are measured inward from the original exposed face; leave the opposite finish intact and do not combine 
opposing deep cuts through the same thin piece.
+Keep end lands and route recesses continuous across module seams without cutting the mating surfaces.
+
+The partition remains 2,500 mm high × 100 mm deep, with 1,800 mm of air above it; “storey-scale” does not mean 
increasing its envelope.
+Keep all partition glass between 450 and 2,100 mm unobstructed.
+The carpet stays level through the room; a partition base is a narrow vertical frame, never a raised room platform.
+The stair helix is cut into the solid core, rather than made opaque on cage glass, to retain the outer walking 
annulus sightline.
+Keep the existing stair core/tread/rail/cage radii of 800 / 2,600 / 2,630 / 2,750 mm.
+
+Keep [Glass_Clear](../../../../docs/systems/GLASS.md) near-clear, with one broad and one thin translucent diagonal 
streak.
+Near-black values belong in cut reveals and grazing edges, without making the panes mirror-dark.
+Dark figures are visible in the concept views; this is a visual review of still images, not proof of gameplay 
readability through two panes.
+
+## 01 · Façade
+
+[Sheet](01_Facade/sheet_r3.png) · **2 image tries**
+
+| Direction and idea | Kit pieces changed | Proposed form moves, mm | Materials |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **A · Folded cobalt piers** — a sharp white knife exposes a cobalt pocket, repeated vertically. | `Column_Facade`, 
`Column_CornerL/R`, head finish of `Window_4m/2m`. | Retain 400 × 240 × 4,300 column bounds; street pocket 160 deep, 
from 660 to 4,160 high, 20 side lands and 140 head land; 280-wide cobalt back and an angled white return. Turn the 
field onto a 200-high head zone within the original bay envelope, cutting at most 80 inward. | Existing 
`Wall_PaperWhite`, `Accent_Cobalt`, `Trim_Navy`; `Glass_Clear` unchanged. |
+| **B · Stacked shadow slots** — white floors become sharp bands over black undercuts. | Street edges of `Slab_*`, 
head finish of `Window_4m/2m`, corner returns. | Inside the 200 slab, cut an 80-high × 120-deep undercut with an 
inclined remaining lip; retain the original leading plane and top skin. Head recess 100 high × 80 deep at 4,200–4,300, 
preserving the contact land. A 10-high cyan line sits at the rear of one selected reveal; a whole cobalt end-bay 
return provides the single large colour field. | Existing white, cobalt and navy; **proposal:** `Light_CyanHairline`. |
+
+**Build A:** the folded pier is the clearer silhouette change without reworking every slab.
+B is the bolder horizontal alternative, with its depth taken from shadow rather than oversized beams.
+
