visual surface only; steps, rail and cage retained. | A 1,000-high helical channel turns once per 4,500 rise, 160 
inward from radius 800 to 640, with 40 bevels. Uncut white lands preserve the original radius and top/bottom contact 
faces. Phase the channel across the storey seam while leaving mating faces intact. No opaque band on the cage; no 
cobalt shelf outside the core; plain full-height red leaf remains. | Existing `Wall_PaperWhite`, `Accent_Cobalt`, 
`Trim_Navy`, `Stair_Aluminium`, `Glass_Clear`, `Door_LockedRed`. |
+
+**Build B:** it is the strongest new landmark in the set and changes the three-floor read without screening the 
walking annulus.
+A is the stronger local locked-route signal; the two concepts are alternatives here, not a recommendation to stack 
both hero treatments.
