+| **A · Floor-to-wall route** — carpet, overhead void and a whole wall return become one route. | Floor finish and 
underside of `Slab_*`, `Slab_Stairwell` approach, existing spine return; recessed visual variant of 
`Ceiling_LightStrip`. | A flush 2,000-wide route uses four 500-wide carpet rows. Above it, a 2,000-wide × 120-deep 
upward soffit slot leaves 80 of the slab above. A 10-wide line sits at its rear. At the stair, the route climbs the 
existing 4,000 × 4,300 wall face with a 120-deep return cut; no step in the floor. | Existing `Floor_Carpet`, 
`Ceiling_Tile`, white, navy and cobalt; **proposals:** `Floor_Carpet_Cobalt`, `Light_CyanHairline`. |
+| **B · Tilted white coffers** — shallow sliced planes cast a strong sawtooth shadow. | Underside of `Slab_*`, with 
existing end-wall finish. | Pockets 2,000 wide ramp upward from 4,300 to 4,440 over 2,000 run: 140 maximum cut, about 
4° slope, 60 minimum skin. White lands remain at the original 4,300 soffit, with the exterior slab edge still 200 
total. Keep the quiet 500 tile grid outside the relief and one whole cobalt end face/return; a 10-wide cyan line is 
limited to one end. | Existing `Ceiling_Tile`, `Wall_PaperWhite`, `Floor_Carpet`, `Accent_Cobalt`, `Trim_Navy`; 
**proposal:** `Light_CyanHairline`. |
+
+**Build A:** the connected floor, void and wall gives players a stronger route than the round-2 carpet stripe.
+B is the more sculptural ceiling option and needs careful control of slab depth when modelled.
+
+## 05 · Glass partition
+
+[Sheet](05_Partition/sheet_r3.png) · **3 image tries**
+
+| Direction and idea | Kit pieces changed | Proposed form moves, mm | Materials |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **A · Folded cobalt corner frame** — a carved L-shaped head makes the clear enclosure a volume. | 
`Partition_Glass_4m/2m` header/base visual variants at the butt-jointed corner. | Upper 400-high mass at 2,100–2,500 
wraps the 4,000 front and 2,000 return; carve 65 into the existing 100 depth, leaving 35 back skin. A white 
knife/chevron stays at the original plane, with cobalt behind it. Lower vertical band is 250 high × 100 deep; no 
opaque element in the 450–2,100 sightline. | Existing `Accent_Cobalt`, `Wall_PaperWhite`, `Trim_Navy`, `Glass_Clear`. |
+| **B · Carved white room box** — white negative cuts frame one cobalt interior face. | Same partition pieces plus 
the existing rear `Wall_Solid_4m_Cobalt` face. | Upper white 400 at 2,100–2,500 has a 70-deep folded cut, retaining 30 
skin. Lower white vertical plinth is 450 high, cut at most 60 into its 100 depth, retaining 40; its narrow top remains 
level. Existing 4,000 × 4,300 rear spine face is cobalt with a 120-deep return. Floor stays continuous and the open 
air above the partition remains 1,800. | Existing white, cobalt, navy and near-clear glass; **proposal:** 
`Light_CyanHairline`, 10 wide in one high pocket. |
+
+**Build B:** the white carved enclosure and cobalt interior are the clearest volume change, with the standing figure 
placed against a pale side return.
+Keep its 2,500 height; do not turn the painted framing into a full-height room or a raised deck.
+
+## Generation and review
+
+**10 built-in ImageGen tries:** façade 2, walls/door 1, stair 2, ceiling/floor 2, partition 3.
+The five revisions corrected façade proportions, inward stair relief, soffit depth, partition height/floor level, and 
partition presentation.
+The [prompt set](prompts_r3.json) contains the exact initial and revision prompts and the selected output for each 
family.
+The contact sheet and thumbnail check are deterministic layouts of the selected renders; they do not repaint their 
contents.
+
+Reviewed all twenty selected views at sheet size and all ten direction columns at 200 px width.
+Checked distinct A/B silhouettes and value patterns, hard shadow edges, cobalt hierarchy, clear figure sightlines, 
three-floor repetition and absence of plants, grime and decorative bars.
+Small relief depths, painted proportions, exact projection, glass sheen strength and camera distances remain concept 
approximations; the numerical targets above govern the models.
+No Unity assets or system behaviour changed, so the existing system docs need no update.
+Round 1, round 2 and the briefs are retained unchanged.
+
+Read-only checks: `Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256` compared all 17 pre-existing brief/round-1/round-2 files with the 
starting hashes; `[System.Drawing.Image]::FromFile(...)` checked each final PNG’s dimensions.
+No automated tests, Play Mode, multiplayer or performance checks were run.
+
